This is a Rust + Android rewrite of backupTW-iOS, treating its Swift
implementation and XCTest suite as the behavioral spec this port's
protocol/business logic is built against (not code copied verbatim,
but heavily informed by it — including, in places, the reasoning
recorded in its own source comments). backupTW-iOS is itself licensed
Apache License 2.0:

  - bonds-tw/backupTW-iOS
    https://github.com/bonds-tw/backupTW-iOS

Bundled certificates (core/assets/*.cer):

  - MOICA-G3.cer and GRCA-G3.cer are public CA certificates published by the
    Ministry of the Interior Certificate Authority (moica.nat.gov.tw) and the
    Government Root Certification Authority (grca.nat.gov.tw). Their SHA-256
    fingerprints are pinned and checked at load time in
    core/src/moica/issuer_certificate.rs.

Third-party crates (Rust, see core/Cargo.lock) and Gradle dependencies
(Kotlin/Java, see android/*/build.gradle.kts) keep their own licenses,
unchanged by inclusion here.
